WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.740
The New York Times did an

00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:04.380
audio interview with Donald Trump, and it's

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:07.060
truly bizarre. And it... it's starting to get

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:09.440
to the point where questions about

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:11.700
Trump's mental and emotional stability

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:15.100
really sort of can't be ignored. Uh, Trump said yesterday

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:17.500
in this interview that... that, ex-excerpts of which were

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:19.375
released by the New York Times,

00:00:19.375 --> 00:00:21.785
that he never would have appointed Jeff

00:00:21.785 --> 00:00:24.535
Sessions to Attorney General if he

00:00:24.535 --> 00:00:26.085
had known that Jeff

00:00:26.085 --> 00:00:29.085
Sessions was going to recuse himself

00:00:29.085 --> 00:00:31.665
from anything Russia related. He

00:00:31.665 --> 00:00:34.255
called that decision by Jeff Sessions, quote,

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:37.080
"very unfair to the President," which thi- this

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:40.240
entire thing of people being fair to Trump is yet another

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:43.085
way in which he's... he's sort of projected the fact

00:00:43.085 --> 00:00:45.955
that everything he's done, really hasn't

00:00:45.955 --> 00:00:48.805
been fair to anyone... the American people, other

00:00:48.805 --> 00:00:51.845
elected officials,... But I'm sort of digressing from

00:00:51.845 --> 00:00:54.755
from the main point about Jeff Sessions. He said

00:00:54.755 --> 00:00:56.505
quote, "Sessions should have

00:00:56.505 --> 00:00:59.055
never recused himself, and

00:00:59.055 --> 00:01:02.005
if he was going to recuse himself, he should have told me

00:01:02.005 --> 00:01:04.915
before he took the job, and I would have

00:01:04.915 --> 00:01:07.625
picked somebody else," which makes

00:01:07.625 --> 00:01:10.185
absolutely no sense on many levels; Number one,

00:01:10.725 --> 00:01:13.615
before Jeff Sessions was selected by Donald Trump,

00:01:13.615 --> 00:01:16.535
I mean, I guess, gi-, given, given

00:01:16.540 --> 00:01:19.095
what appears to be Session's involvement, it's

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:22.380
possible, he could've... he could have, uh, foreseen

00:01:22.460 --> 00:01:25.635
how this entire Trump/Russia thing was going to explode, but

00:01:25.635 --> 00:01:29.600
why would Jeff Sessions have anticipated such a recusal, at the

00:01:29.635 --> 00:01:32.795
very beginning of his selection process, and in addition to that,

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:35.775
Sessions really had no choice but to do that. The guy was

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:38.400
clearly involved in part of the

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:40.315
problem with Trump/Russia,

00:01:40.315 --> 00:01:42.565
not recusing himself... and Trump

00:01:42.565 --> 00:01:45.595
probably is too much of a political novice to even

00:01:45.595 --> 00:01:49.075
realize this, Sessions *not* recusing himself

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:51.880
would probably have cost, uh, *caused* Trump

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:54.680
even more trouble. And Donald Trump

00:01:54.680 --> 00:01:57.255
said, in this interview with the New York Times, that

00:01:57.255 --> 00:02:00.235
it was Sessions' recusal that

00:02:00.235 --> 00:02:03.200
ultimately led to the appointment of Special

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:06.145
Prosecutor, Robert Mueller, which is sort of an

00:02:06.145 --> 00:02:09.285
odd perspective, because it... Tr- Trump seems to be

00:02:09.285 --> 00:02:12.135
operating in a very simplistic world, where;

00:02:12.405 --> 00:02:15.045
If "B" happened after "A"

00:02:15.045 --> 00:02:17.665
it must have been caused by "A". While

00:02:17.665 --> 00:02:19.845
it's true that the Special Prosecutor

00:02:19.845 --> 00:02:21.500
was appointed after

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:24.555
the recusal of Jeff Sessions, there were endless

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:27.605
other factors and reasons that we ultimately ended up

00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:30.380
with a Special Prosecutor, and the recusal of Jeff

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:32.920
Sessions was only part of the broader Russia sca...

00:02:32.925 --> 00:02:35.840
Russia *question*, so to speak. In this same

00:02:35.845 --> 00:02:38.725
*very* odd interview with the New York Times

00:02:38.725 --> 00:02:41.525
Trump went after, not only Jeff Sessions, but

00:02:41.525 --> 00:02:43.315
also went after fired FBI

00:02:43.315 --> 00:02:46.335
Director, James Comey, saying that Comey tried to,

00:02:46.335 --> 00:02:49.005
"leverage a dossier of compromising

00:02:49.005 --> 00:02:52.215
material in order to keep his job."

00:02:52.215 --> 00:02:55.435
Bear in mind that this is the same dossier

00:02:55.435 --> 00:02:57.365
that for a long time Donald Trump

00:02:57.365 --> 00:03:00.265
claimed didn't even exist. Later Trump

00:03:00.265 --> 00:03:03.065
claimed that the contents of the dossier

00:03:03.065 --> 00:03:05.765
were bogus, despite the dossier's

00:03:05.765 --> 00:03:08.485
existence being real, but we've seen

00:03:08.485 --> 00:03:10.975
uh, s- since that point, many

00:03:10.975 --> 00:03:14.005
aspects of that blackmail dossier

00:03:14.005 --> 00:03:16.935
confirmed, and of course, James Comey didn't put the dossier

00:03:16.935 --> 00:03:18.865
together. It was put together by former

00:03:18.865 --> 00:03:21.875
MI6 Operative, Christopher St-uh Christopher Steele.

00:03:21.875 --> 00:03:23.115
But here's the crazy thing...

00:03:23.825 --> 00:03:25.505
If Donald Trump is

00:03:25.505 --> 00:03:28.155
criticizing James Comey, for

00:03:28.155 --> 00:03:31.335
wanting to use a dossier of compromising

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:33.115
information against Donald

00:03:33.115 --> 00:03:36.595
Trump, effectively wanting to "blackmail" Donald Trump...

00:03:36.635 --> 00:03:39.565
Blackmail only works, if the

00:03:39.565 --> 00:03:42.200
dirt you have is true. Trump is

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:45.295
effectively incriminating himself here, by saying, "I don't

00:03:45.295 --> 00:03:48.305
like that Comey tried to use an incriminating report

00:03:48.305 --> 00:03:50.925
about me, against me, to keep his job."

00:03:50.925 --> 00:03:52.555
Whether or not that's true,

00:03:52.555 --> 00:03:55.585
that would only even conceivably be

00:03:55.585 --> 00:03:58.395
a viable strategy, if there's actual

00:03:58.395 --> 00:04:01.235
incriminating information about Donald Trump,

00:04:01.235 --> 00:04:04.185
and Trump just doesn't... Trump doesn't have the

00:04:04.185 --> 00:04:07.145
wherewithal and intelligence to realize,

00:04:07.145 --> 00:04:09.700
that by even making this allegation, he's

00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:12.675
effectively incriminating himself. Uh...

00:04:12.675 --> 00:04:14.535
Donald Trump also criticized, in

00:04:14.535 --> 00:04:17.385
this interview with the New York Times, not only Jeff Sessions,

00:04:17.385 --> 00:04:20.375
not only the fired FBI Director, James Comey, but also

00:04:20.375 --> 00:04:23.000
the acting FBI Director, who tremporarily

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:26.005
replaced James Comey. He also criticized

00:04:26.005 --> 00:04:28.925
the Deputy Attorney General, Rod

00:04:28.925 --> 00:04:31.455
Rosenstein. He slammed Special

00:04:31.455 --> 00:04:33.365
Prosecutor, Robert Mueller,

00:04:33.675 --> 00:04:36.675
and sort of issued, like, a thinly veiled threat to Mueller.

00:04:36.675 --> 00:04:38.200
He actually said, if

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:41.200
Robert Mueller starts looking at Trump's family's

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:43.400
finances, above and beyond

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:46.000
just Russia related stuff, that it

00:04:46.005 --> 00:04:48.735
would cross a "Red Line," which is sort of

00:04:48.735 --> 00:04:51.875
a threat from the President to the Special Prosecutor,  and

00:04:51.875 --> 00:04:54.100
this is the guy that supposedly

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:57.335
is the most loyal, there's no one more loyal than Trump.

00:04:57.335 --> 00:05:00.285
He's rebuking Jeff Sessions. He...

00:05:00.285 --> 00:05:02.805
ya' know, the Flynn thing was a disaster. Trump

00:05:02.805 --> 00:05:05.815
ended up having to force him to resign, uh... but

00:05:05.815 --> 00:05:08.400
Trump also seems completely disconnected for reali...

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:11.485
from reality, because he again insisted, during this

00:05:11.485 --> 00:05:14.480
New York Times interview, that he's not under investigation,

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:17.560
and that ship has long sailed. Trump is quoted

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:20.585
uh... in... in the um...interview as saying,

00:05:20.585 --> 00:05:23.400
"I don't think we're under investigation.

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:26.485
I'm not under investigation. For what? I didn't do

00:05:26.485 --> 00:05:29.500
anything wrong." That ship has sailed, Donny Boy.

00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:31.985
Numerous reports now indicate...

00:05:32.115 --> 00:05:34.985
and they kind of have for close to two months now,

00:05:34.985 --> 00:05:37.485
that Robert Mueller *is* investigating Donald Trump,

00:05:37.485 --> 00:05:40.505
both for his potential role in the collusion or

00:05:40.505 --> 00:05:42.895
coordination with Russia, itself, as

00:05:42.895 --> 00:05:44.800
well as his role in the cover-up,

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:47.615
including potential obstruction of justice.

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:50.515
It... It doesn't seem to me that Donald Trump is even

00:05:50.520 --> 00:05:52.220
capable of, sort of, acting in a way

00:05:52.220 --> 00:05:55.245
that doesn't seem suspicious or erratic,

00:05:55.245 --> 00:05:57.845
and the question I came away with, from listening

00:05:57.845 --> 00:06:00.965
to excerpts from this New York Times interview, is...

00:06:00.965 --> 00:06:03.945
How is Trump even in that room? Who thought it was a

00:06:03.945 --> 00:06:06.200
good idea for Donald Trump to be

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:09.360
interviewed by the New York Times? And a common

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:12.235
trait of total narcissists is that

00:06:12.235 --> 00:06:15.300
they're super confident in their ability

00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:18.000
to say anything they want, because they believe "Anyone

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:21.295
I talk to is going to be persuaded by my perspective,

00:06:21.295 --> 00:06:24.000
and they're going to come away seeing it my way," and

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:26.825
that really appears to be affecting Donald Trump here.

00:06:26.825 --> 00:06:29.800
We know Trump is a terrible legal client, right?

00:06:29.800 --> 00:06:32.435
He doesn't listen to his lawyers. Lawyers worry that

00:06:32.435 --> 00:06:35.445
Trump won't even pay them for their work. But this is

00:06:35.445 --> 00:06:38.355
sort of a new low. Going after his

00:06:38.355 --> 00:06:41.455
own current sitting Attorney General

00:06:41.665 --> 00:06:43.845
and really everybody else. Total lack of

00:06:43.845 --> 00:06:45.200
personal responsibility.

